    "test_pr": 480,
    "problem_statement": "The NimBLE host allows GATT services to be registered and made available only a single time at startup. There is no way to replace the set of supported services after the host has started (e.g. blehostd needs to accept service registration over a socket after the host is already up). The feature requires the host to expose a public function that resets the GATT server to its initial state (removing all supported services, characteristics and descriptors) and a public function that makes the registered services available to peers, both callable on demand. These functions must succeed only when no peers are connected and no GAP procedures (advertise, discover, connect) are active, returning a busy indicator otherwise. The test harness must be able to reset the GATT server, register a new set of services, and start them, replacing the previous one-time startup sequence.",
