    "problem_statement_fixed": "The NimBLE host allows GATT services to be registered and made available only a single time at startup. There is no way to replace the set of supported services after the host has started (e.g. blehostd needs to accept service registration over a socket after the host is already up). The feature requires the host to expose public functions int ble_gatts_reset(void) and int ble_gatts_start(void) in host/ble_gatt.h. ble_gatts_reset must reset the GATT server to its initial state by removing all supported services, characteristics and descriptors. ble_gatts_start must make the registered services available to peers; after it returns success, the GATT server must be in the started state and able to handle peer GATT requests, so that it can be called on demand in place of the one-time startup sequence. On success, both functions return 0. They must succeed only when no peers are connected and no GAP procedures (advertise, discover, connect) are active, returning a busy indicator otherwise. After ble_gatts_reset, a caller may use ble_gatts_add_svcs to register a new service set and then ble_gatts_start to start it, replacing the previous one-time startup sequence."
